# Ctrl+click on the line Copilot prints for a picture it read opens the picture in CST,
# `o` hands it on (refused here, as over SSH), Esc closes it, and a line naming a file
# that is not there says so instead.

size 110x30
arg --mux
session existing-app Existing app session
image_file pics/sample.png 64x32
# As over SSH: the viewer draws half-blocks either way under this pseudo-terminal, and
# `o` must not open a picture viewer on the desktop of whoever runs the script.
env SSH_TTY=1

wait_for Existing app session
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling

# The stub echoes the line back, so it is on screen as Copilot would print it. The path
# is long enough to wrap in the pane, which is the usual case.
type [Image: Image file at path {projects}\pics\sample.png [image/png] 64x32]
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot received: [Image: Image file at path
dump 01-image-line

click_on ctrl+left Image file at path
wait_for sample.png  64x32
dump 02-viewer

press o
wait_for Not opened:
dump 03-open-refused-over-ssh

press esc
wait_gone sample.png  64x32
dump 04-closed

type Viewed image file at path {projects}\pics\missing.png
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot received: Viewed image file at path
click_on ctrl+left Viewed image file
wait_for No picture at
expect_not sample.png  64x32
dump 05-missing-file
